# AI Today Brief — Engineering Rules

A standalone **Next.js 16 (App Router)** product on **Vercel**: a daily curated **AI/engineering brief** (EN primary, UK secondary) plus evergreen technical concept hubs. Strategy = **brief-led product, authority-built architecture**: the daily brief is the hook; every page also builds **topical authority** + **AEO** (being cited by AI engines) in a defensible dev niche. Data and the `fetch→rank→summarize→publish` pipeline live on **Supabase**. Payments via **LemonSqueezy** (Stripe is blocked in UA). Context: `wiki/architecture/mvp-dev-handoff.md`, `wiki/architecture/prototype-to-production.md`.

## Stack facts (hard — verify before assuming)

- **Next.js 16 App Router**, React 19, **TypeScript strict**, **Tailwind v4** (CSS-first `@theme`, no `tailwind.config.js`), Supabase (`@supabase/supabase-js`), **npm** (`package-lock.json` authoritative).
- **`@/*` alias IS used** (→ `src/*`) — Next idiom. (Intentionally reverses the old portfolio "relative-only" rule.)
- **Server Components by default.** `'use client'` only for real interactivity (state, effects, browser APIs). Never ship a secret / service key into a client component.
- **No other routing library** (react-router, tanstack) — App Router file routing only.
- Next 16 has breaking changes vs older training knowledge — when unsure of an API, check `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` (see `AGENTS.md`).

## Engineering mindset

- Think before coding: state assumptions, edge cases, failure modes. Ambiguous? Ask one focused question.
- Smallest change that solves it. No abstraction before it's needed twice.
- Errors are part of the API: every async path / parse / external call has a handled failure mode. Never swallow with an empty catch.
- Read neighboring patterns first; match them over personal preference.
- Comments explain *why*, not *what*.

## TypeScript

- `strict: true` non-negotiable. No `any` (warn-gated). No `as` casts without a one-line reason.
- `unknown` at boundaries; narrow with guards (`isX(v: unknown): v is X`). Any JSONB column is `unknown` until guarded.
- `type` for unions/mapped/conditional; `interface` only for extendable object shapes.
- **No enums** — `as const` objects + derived literal unions. Exhaustive switches end with `default: const _x: never = v`.
- `import type { … }` for type-only. Named exports (default only where a tool demands: route files, `*.config.*`).

## React 19 / Next 16 App Router

- Function components, named exports, PascalCase. Hooks at top, never conditional.
- **Derive, don't sync.** `useEffect` only for real side effects — never to mirror props/state.
- Prefer Server Components + streaming `<Suspense>`. Fetch in server components; **never fetch SEO-critical content client-side**.
- Metadata via `generateMetadata`; static params via `generateStaticParams`; freshness via ISR + `revalidateTag`/`revalidatePath` on publish.
- Mutations via **Server Actions** or route handlers (server) — never write to Supabase from the client.
- Keys are stable IDs, never indices. Accessibility is a feature: semantic HTML, keyboard-reachable, visible focus.

## Styling — Tailwind v4

- Utility-first, **CSS-first config**: design tokens in `src/app/globals.css` via `@theme` (port the prototype token set — Fraunces display + Inter body, category colors, surfaces). No `tailwind.config.js`.
- **No CSS-in-JS, no `clsx`/`tailwind-merge`.** Compose conditional classes with template strings / ternaries.
- Mobile-first; tokens via CSS variables over hardcoded hex.

## Supabase

- Two clients: **server** (route handlers / server actions / pipeline — may use `service_role`, NEVER imported by client code) and **browser** (anon key, read-only public data).
- Generated types via `generate_typescript_types` → `src/lib/database.types.ts`, kept in sync on every schema change.
- Always destructure `{ data, error }` and handle `error` first. `select()` explicit columns (no `select('*')` in prod paths). Filter server-side. Keyset pagination, not `OFFSET`.
- **RLS is the source of truth.** Anon reads **published content only**; raw `articles` are never anon-readable; all writes (subscribe/sponsor/social/sends) go **only** through Edge Functions / server with `service_role`.
- Migrations in `supabase/migrations/` (timestamped). Every `UPDATE`/`DELETE` has an explicit `WHERE`. Re-run `get_advisors` after DDL.

## Routing & i18n

- `/[lang]/…`, `lang ∈ {en, uk}`, **EN primary / UK secondary** (UK = low-competition wedge). Validate lang at the boundary; pass a typed `Lang`.
- Canonical shapes: `/[lang]`, `/[lang]/news`, `/[lang]/news/[category]/[item]`, `/[lang]/category/[slug]`, `/[lang]/[brief]` (daily/pack digest hub), `/[lang]/concepts/[slug]`, dev silos `/[lang]/models|frameworks|mlops|…`, `/[lang]/subscribe|about|advertise`, `/privacy|/terms|/ai-disclosure`.
- Item permalinks nest under their **category** (`/[lang]/news/[categorySlug]/[itemSlug]`), matching the breadcrumb 1:1 — never under the publish-pack slug (`[brief]`), which mixes unrelated stories from the same scan cycle and won't match any category a reader clicked through. `[lang]/[brief]/[item]` is a permanent-redirect shim for pre-2026-07-24 URLs only — do not add new links there. See the 2026-07-24 URL/breadcrumb audit for the full rationale.
- Every user-facing string ships in **both** languages in the same change. `Intl.*` with an explicit locale; never hardcode month names.

## SEO / AEO (core to the product)

- `generateMetadata` per route: title, description, canonical, OG, `hreflang` en/uk/x-default.
- JSON-LD: **`TechArticle`** for evergreen/technical pages, **`NewsArticle`** for brief items, plus `FAQPage`/`HowTo`/`BreadcrumbList`/`Organization`+`WebSite`.
- **AEO/GEO is first-class** (the dev audience lives in Perplexity/ChatGPT): structure for extraction — definition block in the first ~300 words, comparison tables, FAQ blocks, attributed stats. See `.agents/skills/geo-content-optimizer`, `schema-markup-generator`, `technical-seo-checker`.
- `robots.txt` allows AI bots (GPTBot/PerplexityBot/ClaudeBot/Google-Extended). `sitemap.xml` + Google News sitemap + RSS via Next route handlers. Consistent editor byline (Discover + E-E-A-T).
- Never block first paint on Supabase for indexed content (prerender / ISR).

## Content discipline (survival rule)

- Editorial gate: `briefs.status: draft→published` by a human (curation moat + AI Act human-oversight + Google scaled-content-abuse survival). Publish **selected, human-edited** items — never auto-generate dozens of thin pages/day.

## Pipeline (Node, `pipeline/**`)

- Single entry `run-daily.ts`: **fetch → rank → summarize → publish**, each stage its own file; typed structs between stages, no module-level mutable state.
- Partial failure is the default (per-source try/catch, log, continue). Hard-fail only when the result would be invalid. Every external call has a timeout + bounded retry. **Idempotent** re-runs (no duplicate `brief_items`).
- `rank.ts` favors technical depth / source-authority / cross-source / recency / dedup (topical-authority tuned, not audience-of-one). Gemini structured JSON output; validate parsed result as `unknown`.
- Holds the `service_role` key — never `NEXT_PUBLIC_`, never imported under `src/`. Structured logs; never log secrets or full prompts.

## Testing — Vitest (logic scope, ≥70% gate)

- **Runner:** `vitest.config.ts` — coverage ≥**70%** on logic-only `src/lib/*` modules (see `include` / `exclude`). Target **~80%** on new logic so Sonar **new code** (80% on free plan) stays green.
- Co-locate `*.test.ts` next to modules. Mock Supabase at the module boundary; pipeline: fixtures + SDK mocked.
- Before push: `npm run pr:check` (= `ci:check` + typecheck + lint + build). `ci:check` = `test:coverage` + `verify:logic-lcov`.

## Structure & conventions

- `kebab-case.ts` modules, `PascalCase.tsx` components, `useCamelCase.ts` hooks. One responsibility per file. Named exports. Barrels only for genuine public surfaces.
- `@/` for cross-cutting imports; relative within a feature folder.

## Performance & bundle

- CWV budgets: LCP ≤ 2.0s · INP ≤ 200ms · CLS ≤ 0.05. `next/image` with explicit dimensions. Dynamic `import()` for heavy one-screen deps. Tree-shakeable named imports (esp. `lucide-react`).

## Forbidden without explicit discussion

- Other frameworks / routers (we are Next App Router); other meta-frameworks.
- State libraries (Zustand/Redux/Jotai/MobX) — use RSC + server state + URL state + small custom hooks.
- Heavy ORMs (Prisma/Drizzle/Kysely) — use `@supabase/supabase-js` directly.
- CSS-in-JS; `clsx` / `tailwind-merge`.
- A separate backend (Express/Fastify/Nest) — logic lives in Next route handlers / Server Actions / Supabase Edge Functions / the pipeline.
- **Stripe** — UA-blocked; use **LemonSqueezy** (Merchant of Record).
- New dependencies without justification.

## What "Done" looks like

1. `npm run pr:check` green (`ci:check` + `typecheck` + `lint` + `build`).
2. New user-facing strings exist in **both** EN and UK.
3. Indexed routes render real HTML (ISR / prerender), not an empty shell.
4. No client write to Supabase; no `service_role` in the client bundle.
5. No `console.log` left (warn/error only). Comments say *why*.
